{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head c1bfe172173bb5d1c7a960b24741ace2c83b7266 on planner/security-pages-20261111, all six artifacts, for S9, request bc50fc0c, under promise 7e55c418 and review request f958fb3b. The security pages now state what main 9f3338ff does at each point that review 79daff0f found. The head also states the two S5 items in `entry-points.md` and the threat model, as ruling 85abcaa7 asks. Request bc50fc0c gave `entry-points.md` to S1, and that ruling supersedes it.\n\nI checked each new statement against main 9f3338ff:\n\n- Index modes. `apps/room/wrangler.artroom-scope.jsonc` sets `SCOPE_INDEX_MODE` to `register`. `wrangler.jsonc` (dap-self-host), `demo`, `grow`, `lending`, `commons`, `connect` and `celld/wrangler.json` (dap-celld-local) set `enforce`. In `packages/scope/src/scope-index.ts:144-151`, register mode passes an unknown name on to `registerKnown()` on a new target (`packages/scope/src/object.ts:524`).\n- Read-token lifetimes. In the generated native declarations, `read-token` takes `hours` from 1 to 24 in Destination16 and Destination20, and no field in Destination19. `wrangler.commons.jsonc` pins `platform:destination@16` and binds `ARTIFACTS`. `wrangler.connect.jsonc` pins `platform:destination@20` and declares no Artifacts binding.\n- The read mint. `mintRead` in `packages/scope/src/artifacts-host.ts:314-325` never calls `info()`, and it accepts a reply whose `scope` is absent or `read`. The repository read path at line 125 compares `info().remote` first, as `hosts.md` already said.\n- Refusals. `Answer`'s refusal carries `judgedAt: Head` (`packages/contract/src/result.ts:78`).\n- Foreign reads. `PROPOSED_BOUNDS` sets `usesPerEntry` to 128 and `fetchSeconds` to 10 (`packages/contract/src/bounds.ts:110` and `:115`).\n- The census. `scope-index-census.ts:60-73` reads the proof under `PROOF_BYTE_BOUNDS.body`, which is 1 MiB, within `EXACT_PROOF_RECEIVER_BOUNDS.milliseconds`, which is 10,000. It compares the founding actor with the caller only after that read.\n- The tool bridge. The service's `tool` helper (`packages/mcp/src/service.ts:928`) sets no `_meta`, so `create`, `join`, `install_application`, `prepare` and `act` declare no visibility. View tools set it in `packages/mcp/src/views/tools.ts:53`.\n\nI did not trace the Rules statements, the native-mark statements and the foreign-read statements again. They repeat findings 2.2 and 1.7 of review 79daff0f and the planner's rulings on them.\n\nThe tests that read these pages pass on my own extracted copy of the head: `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs` passes 12 of 12, and `scripts/security-settings.test.mjs` passes 3 of 3. The seals, the documented inventory and the threat model's witness names all still parse.\n\nScope. Main 9f3338ff is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the planner's worktree is clean at the head. All six artifacts name the head's commit and their own paths. Against main, the head changes exactly those six paths, all Markdown. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, and the commit-message check passes with 1 checked and 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. On my extracted copy, `check-doc-links.mjs` checks 1,230 local links and finds none broken.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Each page states a limit where an operator or an author looks for it, and the threat model's `verified-genesis` row now names the register-mode path that S2 removes.\n\nSecurity: no new finding. The head changes no code or setting. Several statements describe exposures that remain open: register mode on artroom-scope, 24-hour read tokens on dap-commons, one-admin Rules, and package scripts that can call write tools. S2, S4 and S8 own those changes. When each one lands, its head must correct the same sentences, because these pages say what main does.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One note: the threat model says that \"the other tracked Worker files under `apps/room/`\" select `enforce`. `apps/room/lanes/wrangler.test.jsonc` is a test configuration with no mode. The list of seven names makes the meaning clear.\n\nThis approval authorizes no deployment or setting change.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:15bae66cd43a6bff52b85e41b642c4350c22c437","binding":"assigned","head":"c1bfe172173bb5d1c7a960b24741ace2c83b7266","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:41d3c0aeda91743ae3c5890cbc9231e026da748f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7e55c41822eb7ae98909183742465d2a25308b69\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b8f3f281b4497e85f021170332484f15fbd0454c","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}